//! Seeded random fixture sweep.
//!
//! Where the curated fixtures each target one encoding, the sweep writes many files from
//! randomly generated arrays so that old readers see dtypes, nullability, nesting, lengths,
//! offsets and encoding combinations nobody thought to curate. Every file is deterministic in
//! its seed, so a failure can be regenerated by name.
//!
//! For each seed the sweep writes:
//!
//! - `sweep_<seed>_canonical.vortex`: a random canonical array through the flat layout.
//! - `sweep_<seed>_sliced.vortex`: a random slice of that array, so offsets are non-zero.
//! - `sweep_<seed>_btrblocks.vortex` and `sweep_<seed>_compact.vortex`: the array through the
//!   default and compact compressor pipelines, with randomised row block size and data block
//!   target, so files have many zones and chunks.
//! - `sweep_<seed>_encoded.vortex`: columns of random base arrays (integers, floats, strings,
//!   booleans, timestamps, decimals) each run through a random stack of encoders, then maybe
//!   sliced.
//! - `sweep_<seed>_dict.vortex`, `sweep_<seed>_constant.vortex`, `sweep_<seed>_runend.vortex`:
//!   randomly built encoded arrays through the flat layout.
//!
//! Each written file also gets a set of read-path queries in `queries.json`. A write the target
//! edition rejects, or that panics the writer, is reported and skipped.

